# MTK frame boost scheduler
#

config MTK_FRAME_BOOST
	bool "MTK frame boost scheduler"
	depends on CPU_FREQ && CPU_FREQ_GOV_SCHEDUTIL
	default n
	help
	  A self-contained CPU / GPU / DDR boost scheduler for the MediaTek
	  display path.

	  Say Y here to add a closed-loop boost scheduler that fills in for
	  the missing fpsgo / DVFSRC / PPM performance stack: it keeps a
	  per-cluster CPU frequency floor through the generic PM QoS
	  freq_qos(FREQ_QOS_MIN) interface, re-asserts a GPU OPP floor via
	  mt_gpufreq_target(KIR_POLICY), and raises the DDR / vcore OPP
	  through the MediaTek PM QoS interface.

	  It is driven by an input edge detector and by a userspace request
	  interface at /sys/kernel/frame_boost/.

	  If unsure, say N.
